ist”.","sourceType":"authority_record","title":"LCNAF authority record: Kuckuck, Peter","creator":"Library of Congress","repository":"Library of Congress (LCNAF)","publication":"Library of Congress Name Authority File (LCNAF)","date":"2014","dateRole":"record_creation","dateQualifier":"confirmed","accessDate":"2026-09-23","reliability":"medium","sourceStatus":"verified","primaryUrl":"https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n2014032135","organizationIds":["ORG066"],"personIds":["P020"],"researchNote":"The record establishes a heading for the printed name and cites the film the lyric was written for; it gives no dates, no variant forms and no identification of the author behind the name, which the Library of Congress has not resolved to Fritz Rotter.","researchNoteType":"identity_assessment","authoritySubject":"person","identityRelation":"candidate","slug":"src0892-lcnaf-authority-record-kuckuck-peter","workIds":["W-S080"],"songIds":["S080"],"contributionIds":["CON-S080-L-P020"],"nameVariantIds":["PNV0008"]}],"media":[],"works":[{"id":"W-S080","title":"Mein Gorilla hat ’ne Villa im Zoo","slug":"mein-gorilla-hat-ne-villa-im-zoo","sortTitle":"Mein Gorilla hat ’ne Villa im Zoo","workType":"Song","year":1933,"period":"european","certainty":"confirmed","publicScope":"standalone_page","sourceIds":["SRC0189","SRC0490","SRC0697","SRC0742","SRC0891","SRC0892","SRC0895"],"contributionIds":["CON-S080-C-P009","CON-S080-C-P077","CON-S080-CON-P167","CON-S080-L-P020","CON-S080-LAB-ORG128","CON-S080-P-ORG120","CON-S080-P-P153","CON-S080-PUB-ORG044"],"nameVariantIds":["PNV0008","PNV0019"],"personIds":["P009","P020","P077"],"organizationIds":["ORG044","ORG120","ORG150"],"relationIds":["REL0045"],"songIds":["S080"],"periods":["european"],"mediaIds":["M338"],"publicNote":"The lyric is signed “P. Kuckuck”. Behind the name stood Fritz Rotter, who is credited with the film’s lyrics and who wrote its two other songs under his own name, on prints where Kaper and Jurmann appeared as “Ernst Martin”; the publisher’s house history states that Rotter signed this one number under the pseudonym, in the year all three had to leave Germany. GEMA and the Library of Congress still register Peter Kuckuck as a name of its own."}],"films":[],"songs":[],"otherWorks":[],"titleVariants":[],"workRelations":[],"timelineEvents":[],"places":[],"contributions":[{"id":"CON-S080-L-P020","role":"lyricist","nameAsPrinted":"P. Kuckuck","evidenceContext":"copyright_or_registration","sortOrder":1,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S080"],"personIds":["P020"],"sourceIds":["SRC0153","SRC0189","SRC0490","SRC0891","SRC0892","SRC0895"],"nameVariantIds":["PNV0008"],"scopeNote":"Credited as printed. The pseudonym is identified as Rotter’s in the house history of the firm that holds the song’s surviving salon-orchestra edition, and the film’s lyrics are credited to him; no contemporaneous document names both the pseudonym and the man."}],"personNameVariants":[]}}
